#: ../../../gpu/intel-display/snps-phy.rst:5
msgid "Synopsis PHY support"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu/intel-display/snps-phy:7:
#: ../drivers/gpu/drm/i915/display/intel_snps_phy.c:21
msgid ""
"Synopsis PHYs are primarily programmed by looking up magic register values "
"in tables rather than calculating the necessary values at runtime."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu/intel-display/snps-phy:7:
#: ../drivers/gpu/drm/i915/display/intel_snps_phy.c:24
msgid ""
"Of special note is that the SNPS PHYs include a dedicated port PLL, known as "
"an \"MPLLB.\"  The MPLLB replaces the shared DPLL functionality used on "
"other platforms and must be programming directly during the modeset sequence "
"since it is not handled by the shared DPLL framework as on other platforms."
msgstr ""
